prompt.raw:
My Kotlin service is crashing with a NullPointerException that I can't
reproduce consistently — it seems to happen more under load. I'm also
seeing what might be a resource leak; memory creeps up over time even
though I'm not holding onto data. Can you help me figure out what's
wrong with this code?

```kotlin
class UserService(private val repo: UserRepository) {
    private val scope = CoroutineScope(Dispatchers.IO)

    fun getUser(id: String): UserProfile {
        var result: UserProfile? = null
        scope.launch {
            result = repo.findById(id)
        }
        Thread.sleep(1000)
        return result!!
    }

    fun shutdown() {
        scope.cancel()
    }
}
```

