My TypeScript event processor seems to silently fail sometimes — some
delete operations don't run and I can't tell why, and downstream code
is occasionally crashing on userId values it shouldn't be receiving.
The TypeScript compiler is happy with everything. What's wrong here?

```typescript
async function processEvents(events: unknown[]): Promise<void> {
  const results = await Promise.all(
    events.map(async (event) => {
      const e = event as { type: string; userId: string };
      if (e.type === "delete") {
        await deleteUser(e.userId);
      }
      return e.userId;
    })
  );
  console.log(`Processed ${results.length} events`);
}
```

